-A failed delivery is not retried.
+Each request uses a 5 second timeout. A failed delivery is retried up to 3
+times (4 attempts total) with exponential backoff (1s, 2s, 4s between
+attempts). 5xx responses and connection/timeout errors are treated as
+retryable; 4xx responses are treated as final and are not retried.
+
+On success, `deliver` returns a `DeliveryResult` with the final `status` and
+an `attempts` list recording every attempt made (its number, status code, and
+error, if any). If delivery never succeeds, `deliver` raises `DeliveryError`,
+which carries the same `attempts` list so a caller can see how many attempts
+were made and why each one failed.
